// Which monsters fit which part in a prefab's slot, read by
// `atglyph::rules::role::load`: a map from a role's name to its members' names,
// each a name `monsters.ron` has. A prefab's slot asking for a role draws
// one of its members by the spawn table's own weights, at the slot's own
// band (`src/prefabs.rs`'s doc comment on `Pick::Role`).
//
// `grubnak-honor-guard`: Grubnak the goblin king's own hall stands four
// slots on this role, so his guard is "4 of goblin, archer, conjurer,
// mystic" as the content sheet's row says, each slot drawn on its own
// rather than one of each guaranteed.
{
    "grubnak-honor-guard": ["goblin", "goblin archer", "goblin conjurer", "goblin mystic"],
}
